# CommishDesk engine configuration — reference list of the environment variables
# the engine reads. It reads them from the process environment (`os.environ`)
# only; there is NO .env auto-loading wired yet, so a `.env` file on disk does
# nothing on its own. To use any of the optional settings below, export the
# variable in your shell (or your process manager / CI) before running the CLI.
#
# The engine runs with NONE of these set — zero credentials, no network beyond
# the Sleeper public API. Never commit real values.

# --- Epic 3 LLM narrator (all optional) --------------------------------------
#
# Setting ANY of the provider API keys below (set and non-blank) auto-enables the
# LLM narrator: voiced prose instead of the zero-credential template narrator,
# unless you pass `--no-llm`. `--llm` forces it on even with no key (the adapters
# then fail over to the template). `--league demo` ALWAYS uses the template
# narrator, regardless of any key set here. Leave every variable below unset for
# deterministic, credential-free output. The provider SDKs are an optional
# install: `pip install 'commishdesk[llm]'` (or `uv sync --extra llm`).
#
# Anthropic key for the primary provider. `LLM_API_KEY` is an accepted alias.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#LLM_API_KEY=
#
# Google (Gemini) key for the fallback provider. `GOOGLE_API_KEY` is an accepted
# alias.
#GEMINI_API_KEY=
#GOOGLE_API_KEY=
#
# Override the model per role as "<provider>:<model_id>" (provider is `anthropic`
# or `google`). Defaults: anthropic:claude-sonnet-5 and google:gemini-3.5-flash.
#COMMISHDESK_LLM_PRIMARY=anthropic:claude-sonnet-5
#COMMISHDESK_LLM_FALLBACK=google:gemini-3.5-flash
#
# Optional base-URL override for each role's provider SDK (e.g. a gateway or a
# regional endpoint). Unset means the SDK default.
#COMMISHDESK_LLM_PRIMARY_ENDPOINT=
#COMMISHDESK_LLM_FALLBACK_ENDPOINT=

# Optional. Force the log format: `json` or `human`. Unset (or any other value)
# auto-detects from whether stderr is a TTY.
#COMMISHDESK_LOG_FORMAT=
